<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caguana Ceremonial Site</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Caguana Indigenous Ceremonial Park</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caguana is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a> ceremonial site near Utuado in the central mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>. Its ball courts and plazas, lined with upright stones carved with petroglyphs, were built around the 13th century. Preserved as the Caguana Indigenous Ceremonial Park, it is one of the most important Taíno sites in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>.</p></div>
